=== SURVEY ===

Baseline route + page (must remain canonical when AI is off):
  GET /api/v1/analytics/tco          → internal/api/tco_handler.go (TCOHandler.GetTCO)
  Frontend route /tco (canonical)    → web/src/App.tsx ln 463
  Frontend route /analytics/tco      → not previously mounted; the slice
                                       prompt registered the AI feature
                                       against /analytics/tco, so the
                                       slice must add that path as an
                                       alias to the same TrueCostPage
                                       component (mirrors slice 0029's
                                       /charging/costs alias precedent).
  Page: web/src/features/analytics/pages/TrueCostPage.tsx
  React Query hook: useCostBreakdown in web/src/api/hooks/useAnalytics.ts
  TS interface: TCOSummary in web/src/api/types.ts (matches Go JSON tags)

Wire-shape inventory of the canonical envelope (18 top-level fields +
6-field monthly_breakdown row):
  vehicle_id, total_charging_cost, total_wh, total_sessions, total_km,
  first_date, last_date, months_of_ownership, cost_per_km_ev,
  cost_per_km_ice, equivalent_gas_cost, total_savings, monthly_savings,
  maintenance_savings_estimate, gas_price, gas_efficiency_mpg,
  base_cost_per_kwh, monthly_breakdown[]
Each monthly_breakdown row: month, ev_cost, energy_wh, equiv_gas_cost,
                            savings, cumulative_savings.

Slice-0029 cost-forecast-narration precedent (closest sibling): C4 narrator
that explains a deterministic /analytics/cost-forecast envelope through a
single read-only typed tool (query_cost_forecast). Reused architecture
verbatim:
  - Pure helper in internal/api/ (ComputeCostForecast) shared by the
    canonical handler AND the AI tool's production adapter (no duplicate
    SQL, byte-identical wire shape).
  - Strategy package internal/ai/strategies/cost-forecast-narration/{
    strategy.go, strategy_test.go, goldens.yaml, canned/}.
  - Tool package internal/ai/tools/cost_forecast.go (typed Input + envelope
    + port + RegisterCostForecastNarrationTools).
  - Handler internal/api/ai_cost_forecast_narration_handler.go with
    Production adapter that constructs the envelope from the helper.
  - SPA wrapper web/src/components/ai/AICostForecastNarration.tsx using
    AIFeatureCard + useAiStream + withAiFeature.

Slice-0049 predictive-maintenance precedent: re-uses redact.PolicyDigest()
directly (no new per-feature constructor in policies.go) — adopted that
pattern here so the slice stays strictly within the allowed-files list.

Existing infrastructure consumed (no new ports/decorators added):
  - guard.Wrap (per-feature ai_mode + toggle short-circuit, ADR-015 §I6/§I7)
  - features.Registry (M2 entry with explicit empty Job/Push slices)
  - dispatch.Run (decorator chain assembly + provider call loop)
  - redact.PolicyDigest (Allow=ClassVehicleName, Mode=ModeRedactedTags)
  - tools.Registry (provider-agnostic tool dispatcher)
  - useAiStream (SPA SSE hook: AbortController cleanup, runningRef
    coalescer, Accept text/event-stream)
  - AIFeatureCard (HX shared scaffold with computed disabled, "Ask Helix"
    aria-label composition, AiOutputPanel placement)
  - withAiFeature HOC (renders null when feature absent, ADR-015 §I5)

=== REASONING ===

ADR-015 invariants this slice touches and how each is preserved:

I1 default-off:        Registry entry sets DefaultOn=false. The 9999 final
                       gate's CoverageOK + tier walker proves the entry is
                       complete (Tier="M2", explicit Routes/JobNames/PushKinds).

I3 baseline intact:    The deterministic /analytics/tco handler is unchanged
                       in observable behaviour. The 229-line inline math was
                       extracted into ComputeTCOSummary in a new file
                       (internal/api/tco_summary.go) and the handler now
                       delegates to that helper, but the JSON wire shape is
                       byte-identical (same field names, same math.Round
                       scaling factors, same monthly_breakdown empty-not-nil
                       guard). A new wire-shape contract test
                       (TestComputeTCOSummary_StructFieldsPinWireShape)
                       reflective-locks all 18 + 6 field names to prevent
                       silent drift in future refactors.

I4 zero egress:        The new POST /api/v1/ai/analytics/tco/narrate route
                       is wrapped in guard.Wrap("tco-narration", …); the
                       guard short-circuits to 404 BEFORE the handler runs
                       when ai_mode='off'. No SSE stream is opened, no
                       provider call is made, no fetch leaves the box.
                       The 9999 final gate's egress walker reads this from
                       the registry RouteSet.

I5 hidden UI:          AITCONarration is wrapped in withAiFeature(
                       'tco-narration', InnerSection); the HOC returns null
                       when the per-feature gate is closed, so the entire
                       surface is absent from the DOM (no greyed button, no
                       data-testid). TestTCONarrationAIOffShowsChartsOnly
                       proves this on the React side; the Go-side test of
                       the same name proves the backend 404.

I6 404 routes:         guard.Wrap is the same code path 47 other AI routes
                       use; off-mode surfaces 404 with no feature metadata
                       leaked. The Go test asserts this directly with a
                       canary inner handler that returns 500 if reached
                       (proving the guard short-circuits correctly).

I7 per-feature:        DefaultOn=false. Toggle independence proven by the
                       off-mode test's two negative cases: ai_mode='off'
                       with toggle=true (mode trumps toggle) AND
                       ai_mode='cloud' with toggle=false (toggle gates
                       within enabled mode). Positive control proves the
                       gate actually opens when both are set.

I8 propose-only:       The strategy registers exactly one tool
                       (query_tco_summary) and zero mutating tools. The
                       tool's Mutates() bool returns false. Strategy_test
                       pins the empty MutatingTools list. The narrator
                       has NO write path; the deterministic chart's read
                       endpoint remains the user-facing data source.

I9 redaction:          PolicyDigest (Allow=[ClassVehicleName],
                       Mode=ModeRedactedTags) is installed via the
                       F4↔F8 redactadapter wrap, exactly as
                       cost-forecast-narration / vampire-drain-explanation
                       / period-compare-narration / predictive-maintenance
                       do. Aggregate cost numbers are user-visible by
                       slice-prompt mandate; everything else (VINs,
                       lat/lng, place names, addresses, charger network
                       labels) is converted to round-trip tags before the
                       provider call.

I10 type system:       The tool input is a typed struct with a single
                       VehicleID int64 field plus json+jsonschema validation
                       tags (`required,gte=1`). A bad request fails the
                       validator; the handler-side parser is the second
                       gate (DisallowUnknownFields, VehicleID > 0). The
                       wire-shape contract test pins all 24 JSON keys
                       (18 top-level + 6 monthly_breakdown) so a future
                       refactor of the helper cannot silently drop or
                       rename a field consumed by either the chart OR the
                       AI envelope.

I12 client/bg:         Registry declares JobNames=[] and PushKinds=[]
                       explicitly (not omitted). No new background worker
                       ships in this slice. Service-worker chunk
                       'ai-tco-narration' is reserved for future route-split
                       work but is not written to here. No new client
                       storage keys (the SSE stream is closed on unmount
                       via the hook's AbortController cleanup).

Why select-via-HOC over branch-in-business-logic (P10): the deterministic
TCO chart on TrueCostPage.tsx remains structurally unmodified — every
hero card, area chart, bar chart, savings-breakdown panel renders
identically regardless of AI state. The AI surface is added as a new
sibling component above the existing `tco ?` ternary, and the
withAiFeature HOC is the SOLE switch between "surface exists" and
"surface absent". No business-logic branch on ai_mode anywhere in
TrueCostPage. This matches the cost-forecast-narration precedent.

Why one tool, not two: the entire narration domain is "explain the
deterministic envelope". A second tool ("get_per_session_cost") would
duplicate fields the envelope already exposes via monthly_breakdown.
F7 retrieval is intentionally NOT wired (NeedsRAG=false in the registry
entry) — the deterministic envelope is the single source of ground
truth and contains every aggregate the narrator could need. Adding RAG
would invite hallucinated cross-vehicle context.

Why goldens specifically: typical_growth_savings exercises the
positive-savings dominant case (operating-cost win + assumption
disclosure required); insufficient_data exercises the empty-history
honesty case (no fabricated savings); negative_savings_honesty
exercises the rare-but-load-bearing case where electricity is more
expensive than gas equivalent (no cheerleading, no "buy a gas car"
recommendation). A fourth golden (refusal_other_vehicle) was
considered but dropped — refusal of cross-vehicle requests is a
strategy-test assertion (system-prompt substring pin), not a golden
concern.

